# AccessiBooks - Cursor Development Guide

## Project Overview
AccessiBooks is an accessible multi-format content platform (audiobooks, ebooks, podcasts, magazines) with a 3-tier subscription model, built with React + Express + PostgreSQL.

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React 18 + TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui, TanStack Query v5, wouter (routing)
- **Backend**: Node.js + Express.js + TypeScript, Passport.js (auth), Drizzle ORM
- **Database**: PostgreSQL (Neon), with full-text search (tsvector/tsquery + GIN index)
- **Payments**: Stripe (subscriptions + one-time purchases)
- **Content**: Aggregated from 10+ external APIs (LibriVox, iTunes, Google Books, Open Library, Gutenberg, etc.)

## Project Structure
```
client/src/
  App.tsx              - Main app with routing, auth, header, player orchestration
  pages/               - Page components (library.tsx is the main home view)
  components/          - UI components (book-card, audio-player, ebook-reader, etc.)
  hooks/               - Custom hooks (useAuth, use-subscription, use-purchases, etc.)
  lib/                 - Utilities (queryClient.ts sets up default fetcher)

server/
  index.ts             - Express server entry point
  routes.ts            - All API route definitions (~3700 lines)
  storage.ts           - Data access layer (IStorage interface + ExternalAPIStorage)
  googlePlay.ts        - Google Play Books integration via SerpApi
  contentSources.ts    - External content source fetchers (LibriVox, Standard Ebooks, etc.)
  apiCache.ts          - In-memory LRU cache for external API responses
  vite.ts              - Vite dev server integration (DO NOT MODIFY)

shared/
  schema.ts            - Drizzle ORM schema, Zod validators, shared types
```

## Key Conventions

### Import Aliases
- `@/` → `client/src/` (components, hooks, lib)
- `@shared/` → `shared/` (schema types)
- `@assets/` → `attached_assets/` (static assets)

### Data Flow
1. Schema types defined in `shared/schema.ts` using Drizzle + drizzle-zod
2. Storage methods in `server/storage.ts` (implements `IStorage` interface)
3. Express routes in `server/routes.ts` call storage methods
4. Frontend uses TanStack Query v5 (object syntax only: `useQuery({ queryKey: [...] })`)
5. Default queryFn is pre-configured - queries only need `queryKey` matching the API path
6. Mutations use `apiRequest` from `@/lib/queryClient`, then invalidate cache

### Adding a New Content Source
1. Create fetch/search functions in `server/contentSources.ts`
2. Add to `searchPromises` array in `storage.ts` `searchBooks()` method
3. Register in the `getBooks()` fetch pipeline
4. Create frontend section component or add to existing carousel

### Authentication
- Passport.js with multiple strategies: local, Google, Facebook, GitHub, Microsoft, Auth0
- `useAuth()` hook provides `user`, `isLoading`, `login`, `logout`
- Routes use `isAuthenticated` middleware for protected endpoints

### Subscription Model
- 3 tiers: Free ($0), Plus ($4.99/mo), Premium ($9.99/mo)
- `useSubscription()` hook provides `tier`, `isPremium`, `isPlus`, `upgradeToTier()`
- Individual title purchases: $1.99-$2.99 via `usePurchaseCheckout()`

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS with shadcn/ui components
- Dark mode: `darkMode: ["class"]` with CSS variables in `:root` / `.dark`
- Always use explicit `dark:` variants for colors
- Icons: `lucide-react` for UI, `react-icons/si` for brand logos

## Database

### Schema Changes
- Edit `shared/schema.ts` to add/modify Drizzle models
- Run `npm run db:push` to sync (use `--force` if data-loss warning)
- NEVER manually write SQL migrations
- NEVER change primary key column types

### Full-Text Search
- PostgreSQL tsvector column `search_tsv` with GIN index on `books` table
- Weighted: title=A, author=B, genre=C, description=D
- Auto-update trigger maintains the search vector
- `searchBooksDB()` method in storage for instant search

### Key Tables
- `users` - auth, profile, subscription tier
- `books` - content catalog (seeded + API-fetched)
- `purchases` - individual title purchases
- `user_progress` - playback position tracking
- `reviews`, `playlists`, `playlist_items` - social features
- `referrals`, `referral_credits` - referral system
- `ad_campaigns`, `ad_impressions` - advertising

## Running the Project
- `npm run dev` starts both Express backend and Vite frontend on port 5000
- Backend serves API at `/api/*`, Vite serves frontend
- DO NOT modify `server/vite.ts` or `vite.config.ts`

## Environment Variables
Required secrets (set in `.env` or Replit Secrets):
- `DATABASE_URL` - PostgreSQL connection string
- `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` - Payments
- `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` - Google OAuth
- `SERPAPI_API_KEY` - Google Play Books integration
- `GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY` - Google Books API

## Performance Optimizations
- React.lazy() code splitting for 13+ heavy components
- IntersectionObserver infinite scroll in library grid
- Cursor-based pagination API: `GET /api/books?cursor=&limit=&search=`
- In-memory LRU cache (5000 entries, 100MB max) with tiered TTL
- gzip compression middleware (level 6, 1KB threshold)
- Database indexes on books (title, author, genre, source, contentType, etc.)

## Testing
- The app uses Playwright for UI testing
- Run tests via the testing workflow

## Common Pitfalls
- TanStack Query v5 requires object syntax: `useQuery({ queryKey: ['key'] })`
- `useToast` is from `@/hooks/use-toast`, not from shadcn directly
- Frontend env vars must be prefixed with `VITE_` and accessed via `import.meta.env`
- `<SelectItem>` must always have a `value` prop
- Don't explicitly import React (Vite JSX transform handles it)
- The Vite proxy is already configured - don't add another one
